      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The Leafs have spent July remaking the walls before worrying about the furniture - new management, new coaching, and a roster that looks half-detached from the one that closed the book on last year. <strong>John Chayka's first offseason has landed Sergei Bobrovsky, Darren Raddysh and a swarm of depth pieces - Nick Paul, Jack Roslovic, Colton Sissons, Teddy Blueger and Brandon Duhaime - while Gavin McKenna's arrival has sharpened the long view.</strong> Toronto finished 8th in the Atlantic with 78 points, but that number now matters mostly as a reminder of why the teardown of habits and habits-of-habitability began. The real test is balance: Bobrovsky gives the crease heft, the blue line has been patched, and Matthew Schaefer's \"just enjoy it\" advice to McKenna feels apt for a club trying to grow up in a hurry. <strong>What to watch next is whether the cap still allows one more swing, or whether this is the finished blueprint.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 22, 2026"
      },
