      "league": "MLB",
      "record": "46-55",
      "detail": "5th in AL East",
      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The July sun has done little to warm this club's mood - Toronto has been buried by a month of flat bats and thinner hope. <strong>The Blue Jays were hammered 12-2 by the Rays on Monday night</strong>, their third straight loss and the latest sign that this season is tilting hard the wrong way. At 46-55, fifth in the AL East and 12.5 games back, they are no longer chasing the division so much as trying to keep the wheels from coming off completely. Vladimir Guerrero Jr. and the offense have gone quiet at the worst possible time, and Kevin Gausman's future is already being discussed as the losses pile up. <strong>Tonight's rematch with Tampa Bay at 7:07 p.m. ET is less a measuring stick than a test of whether this team still has any fight left.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 22, 2026"
      },
