        "body": "The Raptors' summer is turning on the margins, and that is where smart teams build an edge. <strong>Jamarion Sharp has turned Summer League into an NBA audition</strong>, giving Toronto a reason to keep watching the back end of the roster while the league waits on the Kawhi Leonard and LeBron James dominoes. The Raptors sit 3rd in the Atlantic Division, but that final mark is only a backdrop now; the real work is in shaping the next version of the club. Immanuel Quickley, RJ Barrett, Scottie Barnes and Jakob Poeltl still give the core weight, yet the search for size, shooting and cheap depth is what will define the next month. <strong>Watch Sharp's bid, and watch whether Toronto adds another live body on a minimum or two-way deal</strong>.",
